[LSIG.2.2.1] `SeriesBackendIntervalPulse` backs `active_fraction`. Its state,
in integer nanoseconds of the monotonic clock:

- the closed intervals $(s_i, e_i)$ in which the slot held `true`, each from
  its rising edge to its falling edge, oldest first, not yet evicted;
- $s_{\mathrm{open}}$, the start of the interval still open, present only while
  the slot holds `true`;
- $T = \sum_i (e_i - s_i)$, the on-time of those closed intervals;
- $W$, the window, from the series declaration.
